<h2>Cloud File Metadata Management System</h2>
<h3>1. System Overview</h3>
<p>The <strong>Cloud File Metadata Management System</strong> is a web-base=
d application designed to efficiently store, organize, search, and manage m=
etadata associated with files stored in cloud storage.</p>
<p>Unlike a conventional file-storage system that primarily focuses on stor=
ing file contents, this system maintains structured metadata such as <stron=
g>file name, file type, file size, owner, upload date, modification date, l=
ocation, tags, permissions, and version history</strong>.</p>
<p>The actual files are stored in <strong>MEGA cloud storage</strong>, whil=
e their metadata is maintained separately in <strong>MongoDB</strong>. This=
 separation enables efficient metadata-based searching and organization wit=
hout repeatedly accessing the cloud-stored files.</p>
<h3>2. Objectives</h3>
<p>The main objectives of the system are:</p>
<ul>
<li>Provide secure user registration and authentication.</li>
<li>Allow users to upload, download, rename, organize, and delete files.</l=
i>
<li>Store and manage detailed metadata for every file.</li>
<li>Provide fast searching and filtering based on metadata.</li>
<li>Implement role-based and file-level access control.</li>
<li>Maintain file and metadata version history.</li>
<li>Integrate cloud storage for actual file storage.</li>
<li>Maintain audit logs of important file activities.</li>
<li>Reduce the time required to locate and manage files.</li>
</ul>
<h3>3. Core Modules</h3>
<h4>User Management</h4>
<p>Handles user accounts and authentication.</p>
<p><strong>Functions:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>User registration</li>
<li>Login/logout</li>
<li>JWT-based authentication</li>
<li>Password management</li>
<li>User roles</li>
<li>Profile management</li>
<li>Authorization</li>
</ul>
<h4>File Management</h4>
<p>Manages the actual file operations.</p>
<p><strong>Functions:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Upload files</li>
<li>Download files</li>
<li>Rename files</li>
<li>Delete files</li>
<li>Create folders/categories</li>
<li>Move and organize files</li>
<li>Generate file identifiers</li>
</ul>
<h4>Metadata Management</h4>
<p>Maintains information related to files separately from their contents.</=
p>
<p><strong>Example metadata:</strong></p>
<pre><code class=3D"language-text">File Name
File Type
